    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate leaning heavily on **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, our premier start with an elite score of 80.13. His matchup against Dobbins is ideal, bolstered by a 14% boost from a favorable platoon split and the substantial value added by his position in the leadoff spot. Alongside him, **Yordan Alvarez** (62.19) and **Kyle Schwarber** (61.18) provide high-floor stability; while **Yordan Alvarez** contends with a 3.57 xERA pitcher, his elite xwOBA of 0.465 makes him a must-start regardless of the arm on the mound. **Junior Caminero** also clears the 60-point threshold, benefiting from a high-order placement that offsets his moderate park factors.\n\nStrategic decisions for today\u2019s lineup were driven by our prioritization of stolen base threats and game cap management. **Caleb Durbin** remains a crucial fixture in the lineup; while his raw score sits at 47.16, the combination of a slow opposing delivery and his status as an elite SB threat necessitates his inclusion despite the sub-50 rating. Conversely, **Dillon Dingler** (37.83) and **Chase Meidroth** (37.53) were the most difficult exclusions. Both fell below our strict 40.0 floor, with **Dillon Dingler** suffering specifically from a dynamic platoon penalty that neutralized his park-adjusted upside. \n\nWe are monitoring the risk associated with **Gary Sanchez**, whose score of 41.99 is heavily suppressed by a difficult matchup against Skubal\u2019s 2.77 xERA. While **Gary Sanchez** is technically active, his performance is the most susceptible to a total shutout today. We are also wary of the matchups for **Kazuma Okamoto** and **Colt Keith**, both of whom are facing mid-3.00 xERA arms. We will keep a close eye on any late-inning defensive shifts that might impact **Carson Benge** or **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, both of whom are currently hovering in the marginal 50\u201357 range and will be the first candidates for benching should their game scripts turn stagnant.",
